Requirements
------------

- Qt 6.8 or later, with the Qt Qml and Qt HTTP Server modules
- zlib

Build and run
-------------

$ git clone https://github.com/qt-users-jp/silk.git
$ cd silk
$ qmake
$ make
$ ./bin/silk
silk is running on 8080

To listen on a UNIX domain socket instead of a TCP port (e.g. behind a reverse proxy),
pass --listen.socket or set it in silkconfig.qml:

$ ./bin/silk --listen.socket /run/silk/silk.sock

    listen: Listen {
        socket: '/run/silk/silk.sock'
    }

Changes in Qt 6 that affect silk applications
---------------------------------------------

- XMLHttpRequest no longer reads local files by default. Run silk with the
  environment variable QML_XHR_ALLOW_FILE_READ=1 if your QML pages need it.
- JavaScript files are served as text/javascript instead of application/javascript.
  Use the new name in the deflate configuration if you listed the old one.
- Response header names are sent in lower case. HTTP header names are case-insensitive.
- Injecting signal parameters into handlers, e.g. onMessage: console.log(message),
  is deprecated and prints a warning. Declare them instead:
  onMessage: function(message) { console.log(message) }
